    "body":  {
                 "storage":  {
                                 "value":  "\u003cp\u003eRules for billing if POD is deactivated in one contract and \u0026bdquo;period to\u0026ldquo; in billing data is greater than the deactivation date:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf billing data exists, but POD is deactivated in current contract\u003c/p\u003e\u003col start=\"1\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eone contract before period end date of the billing data and POD is not activated in another contract/another contract version: \u003cstrong\u003ereturn error for the invoice slot\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003col start=\"2\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf billing data exists, POD is deactivated in one contract before period end date of the billing data, but POD is activated in another contract and there is no gap between POD activation/deactivation dates in both contracts\u003ca\u003e[TK1]\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003ca\u003e[TK2]\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003ca\u003e[TK3]\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003ca\u003e[TK4]\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp; (ignore billing run initial filters):\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026middot;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; \u003cem\u003eif applicable level is customer, contract - Exact contract versions should be taken and should be invoiced all PODs from another contract version. Recheck this logic for newly added PODs from new contract versions; If applicable level is POD \u0026ndash; should take only selected POD ;\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026middot;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; \u003cem\u003eIf pod deactivation date is more than max date and billing data is received until max date should \u003cstrong\u003ereturn an error\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003e\u003cu\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003col start=\"3\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf there is not contract valid version for defined period which is covered by billing data by profile/scale with both types of price components (by scales, by profile) \u003cstrong\u003eshould distribute volumes in both contracts according activation/deactivation dates (considering group of price component to intersect billing data period)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003col start=\"4\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn all other cases invoice in latest contract all billing data from all old contracts\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003col start=\"5\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eInterim deduction/generation should discuss\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003col start=\"6\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf billing data by profile will be splitted or merged and it has error condition(point1) \u0026ndash; original header should be error in chain(overrides, merged data)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003col start=\"7\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAll conditions should work after merging and splitting\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003col start=\"8\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBefore pulling contract should be checked POD measurement type\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGeneral rule for billing data\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWithin one billing run if for POD there is different measurement type in initial or pulled contracts should \u003cstrong\u003ereturn warning message \u003c/strong\u003efor all billing data for this POD and skip all billing data, invoice slots in which this POD is added will not be failed;\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eo\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; Should apply this check after invoice slot generation\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eo\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; Reversing pulling logic should be done also for regular pulling\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eo\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; in SLP flow before new contracts pulling should check for all PODs measurement types between old contracts and new pulled contracts \u0026nbsp;and if it is different from existing ones shouldn\u0026rsquo;t pull this contracts , return warning message for old contracts ;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026sect;\u0026nbsp; Fail whole chain of pulling contracts\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026sect;\u0026nbsp; Check again initial contract data and unlock incorrectly locked PODs\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003chr /\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003ca\u003e[TK1]\u003c/a\u003eWihtout gaps\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003ca\u003e[TK2]\u003c/a\u003ePull contract which covers POD act/deact periods\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003ca\u003e[TK3]\u003c/a\u003eExact contract versions should be taken and should be invoiced all PODs from another contract. Recheck this logic for newly added contract versions\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003ca\u003e[TK4]\u003c/a\u003eIf pod deactivation date is more than max date and billing data is received until max date should return an error\u003c/p\u003e",
                                 "representation":  "storage",
