both types of price components (by scales, by profile) \u003cstrong\u003eshould distribute volumes in both contracts according activation/deactivation dates (considering group of price component to intersect billing data period)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003col start=\"4\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn all other cases invoice in latest contract all billing data from all old contracts\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003col start=\"5\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eInterim deduction/generation should discuss\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003col start=\"6\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf billing data by profile will be splitted or merged and it has error condition(point1) â original header should be error in chain(overrides, merged data)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003col start=\"7\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAll conditions should work after merging and splitting\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003col start=\"8\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eBefore pulling contract should be checked POD measurement type\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp\u003eÂ \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eÂ \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eÂ \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eÂ \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGeneral rule for billing data\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWithin one billing run if for POD there is different measurement type in initial or pulled contracts should \u003cstrong\u003ereturn warning message \u003c/strong\u003efor all billing data for this POD and skip all billing data, invoice slots in which this POD is added will not be failed;\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eoÂ Â  Should apply this check after invoice slot generation\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eoÂ Â  Reversing pulling logic should be done also for regular pulling\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eoÂ Â  in SLP flow before new contracts pullin